From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] misc: fastrpc: stay in the call across system sleep

A call from user space waits for the DSP in an interruptible sleep. The
freezer wakes it with a fake signal, the ioctl returns -ERESTARTSYS, and
after the wake it starts over and sends its message to the DSP again while
the first one is still being handled there.

hexagonrpcd's listener (the adsp_listener next2 call, which waits for the
DSP to ask for a file) is always in such a call. On the Retroid Pocket Duo
(SM7750), with the sensors running, each wake crashed the ADSP:

  fatal error received: err_qdi.c:1215:EF:qsh_process:0x4:
  listener_hexagon.c:326:Assertion prevCtx == notify failed

and the sound card did not come back from its restart.

Wait in a freezable state instead: the freezer leaves the task where it is
and the call goes on after the wake. Signals still end the wait.
---
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -1444,7 +1444,8 @@ static inline int fastrpc_wait_for_response(struct fastrpc_invoke_ctx *ctx,
 		if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&ctx->work, 10 * HZ))
 			err = -ETIMEDOUT;
 	} else {
-		err = wait_for_completion_interruptible(&ctx->work);
+		err = wait_for_completion_state(&ctx->work,
+						TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE | TASK_FREEZABLE);
 	}
 
 	return err;
